{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"normalized":[{"fromencoded":false,"from":"File:Regional_Training_Institute.png","to":"File:Regional Training Institute.png"},{"fromencoded":false,"from":"File:6_Ranger_Battalion_Shoulder_Sleeve_Insignia.svg","to":"File:6 Ranger Battalion Shoulder Sleeve Insignia.svg"},{"fromencoded":false,"from":"File:USA_-_17_ABN_DIV.svg","to":"File:USA - 17 ABN DIV.svg"},{"fromencoded":false,"from":"File:CyberCOE_SSI.png","to":"File:CyberCOE SSI.png"},{"fromencoded":false,"from":"File:71st_BfSB_SSI.jpg","to":"File:71st BfSB SSI.jpg"},{"fromencoded":false,"from":"File:29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg","to":"File:29th Infantry Brigade SSI.svg"}],"pages":[{"pageid":4066009,"ns":6,"title":"File:29th Infantry Brigade SSI.svg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2008-05-17T20:34:00Z","user":"Fvasconcellos","size":1582,"width":178,"height":265,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg/330px-29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":322,"thumbheight":480,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg/960px-29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg/330px-29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":322,"height":480,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg/960px-29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2e/29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:29th_Infantry_Brigade_SSI.svg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=4066009","sha1":"c39d27974da21c0835731e9db71d468003a966b7","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2008-05-17 20:34:00","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"29th Infantry Brigade SSI","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"With insignia|PD US Army USAIOH|Valid SVG created with Inkscape:Emblems|US Army Infantry Brigade Shoulder Sleeve Insignia","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoulder_Sleeve_Insignia_(US_Army)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (US Army)\">Shoulder Sleeve Insignia</a> of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/29th_Infantry_Brigade_Combat_Team_(United_States)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:29th Infantry Brigade Combat Team (United States)\">29th Infantry Brigade Combat Team (United States)</a>.\n</p>\n<dl><dt>Description</dt></dl>\n<ul><li><i>On a white shield with arched top and bottom, 2 inches (5.08cm) in width, a blue barbed cross, in base two wavy bars - red and blue conjoined but separated from the cross, and bordered by a white fimbriation 1/16 inch (.16cm) wide all within a 1/8 inch (.32cm) blue border.</i></li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Symbolism</dt></dl>\n<ul><li>The colors blue and white are used for Infantry. The blue cross is suggested by Hawaii's nickname \"Crossroads of the Pacific,\" and the barbed ends represent the protective mission of the Brigade. The red and blue conjoined bars in conjunction with the white appear on the Hawaiian Flag, and also on the Hawaiian Coat of Arms. The bars are wavy to allude to the geographical location of Hawaii as being overseas from the continental United States.</li></ul>\n<dl><dt>Background</dt></dl>\n<ul><li>The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for the 29th Infantry Brigade on 16 May 1968.  It was redesignated for the 29th Infantry Brigade Combat Team with the description and symbolism updated on 18 December 2007.</li></ul>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2008-05-17","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"Own work, after <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.tioh.hqda.pentagon.mil/Inf/29InfantryBrigadeCombatTeam.htm\">the Army Institute of Heraldry</a>.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Fvasconcellos\" title=\"User:Fvasconcellos\">Fvasconcellos</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Permission":{"value":"<i>This image shows a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/flag\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:flag\">flag</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/coat_of_arms\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:coat of arms\">coat of arms</a>, a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/seal_(device)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:seal (device)\">seal</a> or some other official <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/insignia\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:insignia\">insignia</a></b> produced by the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Army_Institute_of_Heraldry\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:United States Army Institute of Heraldry\">United States Army Institute of Heraldry</a></b>.  It is in the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/public_domain\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:public domain\">public domain</a></b> but its use is restricted by <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/pkg/USCODE-2010-title18/pdf/USCODE-2010-title18-partI-chap33-sec704.pdf\">Title 18, United States Code, Section 704</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/18/704\">[1]</a> and the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.gpo.gov/fdsys/granule/CFR-2012-title32-vol3/CFR-2012-title32-vol3-part507/content-detail.html\">Code of Federal Regulations (32 CFR, Part 507)</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.ecfr.gov/cgi-bin/text-idx?mc=true&amp;node=pt32.3.507&amp;rgn=div5\">[2]</a>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/32/part-507\">[3]</a>.  Permission to use these images in the USA for most commercial purposes must be obtained from The Institute of Heraldry prior to their use.</i>","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"insignia","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/svg+xml"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1039778614,"parentid":1039777863,"timestamp":"2025-06-03T17:07:08Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n{{Information\n|description={{W|Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (US Army)|Shoulder Sleeve Insignia}} of the {{w|29th Infantry Brigade Combat Team (United States)}}.\n;Description\n*''On a white shield with arched top and bottom, 2 inches (5.08cm) in width, a blue barbed cross, in base two wavy bars - red and blue conjoined but separated from the cross, and bordered by a white fimbriation 1/16 inch (.16cm) wide all within a 1/8 inch (.32cm) blue border.''\n;Symbolism\n*The colors blue and white are used for Infantry. The blue cross is suggested by Hawaii's nickname \"Crossroads of the Pacific,\" and the barbed ends represent the protective mission of the Brigade. The red and blue conjoined bars in conjunction with the white appear on the Hawaiian Flag, and also on the Hawaiian Coat of Arms. The bars are wavy to allude to the geographical location of Hawaii as being overseas from the continental United States.\n;Background\n*The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved for the 29th Infantry Brigade on 16 May 1968.  It was redesignated for the 29th Infantry Brigade Combat Team with the description and symbolism updated on 18 December 2007.\n|date=2008-05-17\n|source=Own work, after [http://www.tioh.hqda.pentagon.mil/Inf/29InfantryBrigadeCombatTeam.htm the Army Institute of Heraldry].\n|author={{U|Fvasconcellos}}\n|permission={{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n{{Insignia}}\n|other fields={{Igen|Inkscape|+|s=em}}\n}}\n\n[[Category:US Army Infantry Brigade Shoulder Sleeve Insignia]]"}}}]},{"pageid":4094194,"ns":6,"title":"File:171STINFBDE.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2008-05-23T07:51:15Z","user":"Nobunaga24","size":20479,"width":200,"height":304,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0f/171STINFBDE.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":316,"thumbheight":480,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0f/171STINFBDE.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":316,"height":480},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0f/171STINFBDE.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:171STINFBDE.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=4094194","sha1":"11080d389a2921cf3ae95c4926440c971c54a5fa","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2008-05-23 07:51:15","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"171STINFBDE","source":"mediawiki-metadat